# WARM-ALL cells on the EP-G workload. Format: arm n seed tag
#
# THESE ARE THE GATE'S HELD-OUT TEST (D151 (6), D154 (2)).
#
# D156 (4) ADDS A REQUIREMENT THESE CELLS DID NOT CARRY WHEN I FIRST WROTE THEM: the held-out
# cells must run with PER-FRAME UPLOAD (upload-pf), while the FIT cells stay on upload-30s.
# So each cell below needs `--robot-upload per-frame` (34a4af0) in addition to EPG_ARGS. The
# driver's tag mechanism has no per-frame tag, so this needs either a new tag or the flag
# appended for these cells specifically; flagged to the H100 rather than assumed.
#
# NOTE THE CONSEQUENCE, because it is deliberate and not an oversight: the two halves of the
# split now differ in TWO things, the dashcam format AND the upload contract. That is the user's
# design: the held-out test is the workload v5 actually runs, not a minimal perturbation of the
# fit. It means a held-out failure does not localise to one of the two changes, and the p90
# error is the number reported either way.
#
# Per-frame upload makes the believed holding grow every 2 s instead of every 30 s, so
# incrementally-materialising arms find work on far more epochs: warm-all-lru measured 180 to
# 588 prefill pieces (3.27x) and v5-rules 330 to 1,163 (3.52x) on the same cells. At 16 devices
# over 1,200 s that is the number to watch for saturation.
#
# D97 eligibility must be RECOMPUTED for per-frame cells: eligibility.py:94 reads
# robot_history_batches, which is 14.6x larger under per-frame on the same definition, so a
# per-frame cell's entry table must not be read off a committed one. The fit is WARMALL_CELLS_1F on the
# dashcam-1f workload. Nothing fitted there may be reported as a gate pass; the gate passes or
# fails on THESE cells, and MARGIN_CF is then set once from the held-out p90 absolute error.
#
# Ordered so the essential comparison runs first. The first two mirror the 1F fit arm for arm,
# which is what makes this a like-for-like held-out test rather than a different experiment:
warm-all-lru 16 4 _L3
warm-all-lru-reactive 16 4 _L3
#
# Then the control, which should collapse toward the no-warming baseline. If it does not, the
# warming is not what separates the first two arms:
warm-all-lru-off 16 4 _L3
#
# Then the capacity cell, and ONLY the warm-ahead arm can carry it. The reactive arm's peak
# residency is 33,103 tokens against the P1 simulation's 62,736 to 62,916, because it builds only
# histories that already have a pending question, so its kv0.25 cell is valid for the COST-MODEL
# question and must NOT be read as the 0.25x capacity result. warm-all-lru warms every open
# session, so it is the arm that can be capacity-bound at all:
warm-all-lru 16 4 _kv0.25_L3
#
# All four with the belief corrector in its DEFAULT observe mode (leave LIVE2_BELIEF_CORRECTION
# unset), so they stay comparable with the handful. Per-cell check: belief_corrections_observed_only
# MUST equal belief_corrections_changed, else the mutation was applied and the cell is not observe.
#
# EXPECT warm-all-lru to push the 62,944-token pool far harder than anything run so far; there is no
# live number for it. Saturation is a FINDING, not a failed cell: record it rather than retrying.
